The task "TakeBusToWorkCommute" is directly linked to the end of the task graph without considering other commute reasons because it specifically represents a daily routine action. In this context, once the user has taken the bus to work as part of their daily commute, there's no need to consider other travel-related tasks like flying, getting somewhere else, or general travel. The commute is a one-way trip with the end being arrival at work, after which the day progresses normally until the end of the workday when "GoHome" would be triggered.

To ensure proper dependency and logical flow, each task should have dependencies on other relevant tasks. For instance:

- "TakeBusToWorkCommute" could depend on "GetSomewhere" if getting to a bus stop is part of the commute.
- It could also indirectly relate to "Travel" as taking a bus is a form of travel.

